# Dialog System Patterns

## Dialog Structure

1. Save `$savedCursorVisible = $script:CursorVisible`
2. Calculate centered position
3. Queue shadow via `Write-DialogShadow` + dialog content via `Write-Buffer`
4. `Flush-Buffer` to paint
5. Enter input loop (handle keys, clicks, resize)
6. On resize: `Invoke-ResizeHandler` -> `Write-MainFrame -Force -NoFlush` -> optional `& $ParentRedrawCallback` -> queue dialog redraw -> `Flush-Buffer -ClearFirst`
7. Return `@{ Result = $data; NeedsRedraw = $bool }`
8. `Clear-DialogShadow` + clear area via `Write-Buffer` + `Flush-Buffer`
9. Restore `$script:CursorVisible = $savedCursorVisible`

## Never `clear-host` Inside a Dialog

The caller uses `Reset-PostDialogState` (sets `$forceRedraw`). The main loop's buffer-before-clear pattern handles screen clearing.

## Dialog Button Bounds Cleanup (CRITICAL)

All dialogs must clear `$script:DialogButtonBounds = $null` and `$script:DialogButtonClick = $null` in cleanup. Stale bounds block all menu item clicks.

## Parent Chain Redraw (Sub-Dialogs)

Sub-dialogs (Time, Movement from Settings) accept `[scriptblock]$ParentRedrawCallback`. On resize:

```text
Write-MainFrame -Force -NoFlush -> & $ParentRedrawCallback -> queue sub-dialog -> Flush-Buffer -ClearFirst
```

## Scope-Chain Shadowing (CRITICAL)

Scriptblock callbacks run in the caller's scope, not the definer's. Save values with unique prefixed names (`$_stg*`) and shadow conflicting names as locals in the callback.

## Click Detection

Uses `PeekConsoleInput` MOUSE_EVENT records with exact character cell coordinates. Hit-testing uses exact character cell matching — no tolerance, no pixel math.

## Shared Rendering Helpers (use instead of hand-drawing)

### `Invoke-DialogResize` (`Private/Helpers/Invoke-DialogResize.ps1`)

Wraps the resize skeleton used in all 8 dialogs. Parameters: `-HostWidthRef`, `-HostHeightRef`, `-ScreenState`, `-RedrawCallback`, `-ParentRedrawCallback`. All dialogs must use this instead of inlining the resize sequence.

```powershell
Invoke-DialogResize -HostWidthRef ([ref]$localW) -HostHeightRef ([ref]$localH) `
    -ScreenState "dialog-settings" -RedrawCallback { param($w,$h) <draw dialog at new size> } `
    -ParentRedrawCallback $settingsParentRedraw
```

### `Write-DialogButton` (`Private/Rendering/Write-DialogButton.ps1`)

Renders a single dialog button (brackets → emoji + separator → paren/hotkey/suffix) using `DialogButton*` theme variables. Returns the rendered width for accurate click-bound math.

```powershell
$btnW = Write-DialogButton -X $btnX -Y $btnY -Hotkey "a" -Suffix "pply" `
    -Emoji $checkmark -EmojiColor $script:TextSuccess `
    -TextColor $script:DialogButtonText -BgColor $script:DialogButtonBg `
    -HotkeyColor $script:DialogButtonHotkey
```

### `Write-DialogFrame` (`Private/Rendering/Write-DialogFrame.ps1`)

Queues top border, title row, standard divider (Y+2), and bottom border. Content rows are the caller's responsibility. Uses `-NoDivider` to skip the Y+2 divider when the dialog has a custom title row.

```powershell
Write-DialogFrame -X $dialogX -Y $dialogY -Width $dialogWidth -Height $dialogHeight `
    -Title "Confirm Quit" -BorderFG $script:QuitDialogBorder `
    -TitleFG $script:QuitDialogTitle -BG $script:QuitDialogBg
```

